mk('meta-verified-support-links-directory','Meta Verified Support Links Directory (2026): Where Subscribers Get Help','Meta Verified support links','Official Meta Verified links: subscribe, manage, and reach subscriber support, and what support can and cannot do for a disabled account. Checked November 2026.','Meta Verified: official support links','Where Meta Verified subscribers get help, and what to expect from it.','<strong>Meta Verified support is opened from Accounts Center while you are logged in.</strong> It can help with account access and security questions, but it does not reverse a disabled-account decision on request. If the account is already disabled, use the appeal on the notice first. Meta makes the final decision.',[('Subscribe','Accounts Center.'),('Support','Logged-in subscribers.'),('Disabled','Appeal on the notice.')],'',[('mv','Official links',MV)],[BEFORE,SEND],DIRS+', '+L('meta-verified-support-how-to-use','how to use Meta Verified support')+', '+L('meta-verified-account-disabled-support-cannot-help','support cannot help with a disabled account')+'.',[('Can Meta Verified support restore a disabled account?','It cannot override an enforcement decision on request. The appeal on the notice is the route.'),('Can I subscribe after my account is disabled?','You need to be logged in to subscribe, which a disabled account usually cannot do.'),('Is there a Meta Verified phone number?','Support is offered through chat or email inside Accounts Center for subscribers.')]),
notice('facebook-confirm-your-identity-notice','Facebook','Confirm your identity','“Confirm Your Identity” on Facebook: What to Do (2026)','Facebook wants proof that a real person owns the account. It may ask for an ID photo, a video selfie or a code.','<strong>“Confirm your identity” is a check, not a ban.</strong> Upload a clear photo of an accepted ID that matches the name on the profile, or record the video selfie on your usual device. Upload once and wait. Repeated uploads do not speed it up. Meta makes the final decision.',['Use your usual phone or computer.','Photograph the whole ID, flat, in good light.','Make sure the name matches the profile.','Submit once and wait.'],[('My name on Facebook differs from my ID. What now?','Upload the ID anyway. Meta’s ID list allows some documents that show a nickname or other name.'),('Is it safe to upload my ID?','Only on Facebook’s own screens. Never send ID to anyone who messages you.')]),
notice('instagram-we-detected-unusual-activity-notice','Instagram','We detected unusual activity','“We Detected Unusual Activity” on Instagram: What to Do (2026)','Instagram noticed a login or actions that look unlike you, such as a new location, a VPN or fast following. It locks some actions until you confirm it is you.','<strong>“We detected unusual activity” usually means a security check, not a ban.</strong> Confirm with the code sent to your email or phone, then change your password and check Accounts Center for unknown logins. Turn off any VPN and stop automation tools. Instagram makes the final decision.',['Enter the code on your usual device.','Change your password.','Remove unknown devices in Accounts Center.','Turn off VPNs and growth or automation tools.'],[('Will my account be disabled?','Not from this notice alone. Ignoring repeated checks can lead to a suspension.'),('The code never arrives. What now?','See the lost access to email or phone guide.')]),
